# A transcript in the format the monitor port emits: "> " towards the
# controller, "< " from it, "* " the bridge's own commands. Lines beginning
# with # are notes and are not replayed.
#
# THIS ONE IS SYNTHESISED, not captured. It encodes the GRBL 1.1 interface
# documentation: the Ov: block - and the A: field with it - is printed every
# tenth status report when idle, every twentieth while moving, and immediately
# whenever an override or accessory state changes. A: is appended only when
# something is actually on.
#
# To replace it with a real one, set grbl.monitor_port on the appliance and
# capture a cut:
#
#     nc laserbridge.local 2323 > backend/internal/grbl/testdata/your-machine.transcript
#
# A captured file is worth more than this one: it is what a controller did,
# rather than what we believe controllers do.
> $I
< [VER:1.1h.20190825:]
< [OPT:V,15,128]
< ok
> ?
< <Idle|MPos:0.000,0.000,0.000|FS:0,0|Ov:100,100,100>
> G0X10Y10
< ok
# A rapid. The laser is off during it, so no A: even in the report that
# carries Ov: - and that absence is the only reason absence can be read.
> ?
< <Run|MPos:2.100,2.100,0.000|FS:3000,0>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:5.400,5.400,0.000|FS:3000,0>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:9.800,9.800,0.000|FS:3000,0>
> M4S450
< ok
> G1X60F800
< ok
# The cut. The output comes on, which is a change, so the block is forced out
# at once rather than waiting for the counter.
> ?
< <Run|MPos:12.400,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450|Ov:100,100,100|A:S>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:14.900,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:17.300,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:19.800,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:22.200,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:24.700,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:27.100,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:29.600,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:32.000,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:34.500,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:36.900,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:39.400,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:41.800,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:44.300,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:46.700,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:49.200,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:51.600,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:54.100,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
> ?
< <Run|MPos:56.500,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450>
# Twenty reports later, the counter runs out and the block comes round again.
> ?
< <Run|MPos:59.000,10.000,0.000|FS:800,450|Ov:100,100,100|A:S>
> M5
< ok
# The output goes off. A change, so the block is forced out again - this time
# without A:, which is the controller saying nothing is on.
> ?
< <Idle|MPos:60.000,10.000,0.000|FS:0,0|Ov:100,100,100>
